{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137056-a-question-about-boosting-attributes-using-life-3","id":1137056,"title":"A question about boosting attributes using life 3.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-03T15:10:00-07:00","id":1137056,"title":"A question about boosting attributes using life 3.","content":"So, you can boost attributes with life 3. As long as it's within the human's body capabilities (upto 5 dots), its coincidental.<br /> Above that, and it becomes vulgar. Now, if it's permanent it causes genetic flaws and so on, however, if I give myself 10 dex for one day per say, I would get paradox, however there would be no genetic flaw, correct?<br /> And the book also mentions that boosting your attributes too much would cause your body to change in an odd way; giving yourself 10 str per say would make you muscular as fuck, ridiculously so - is that how it works? or that also only happens if the change is permanent?<br /> <br /> Basically I want to know what other consequences are there for boosting your attributes above 5, except for paradox. (Note that I'm not talking about a permanent boost, max 1 ic day, perhaps even just a scene.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T17:10:29-07:00","id":1137126,"title":"","content":"1) No, you would not get Genetic Flaws for an Effect that is temporary. It's only for permanent Effects (which would probably mechanically be symbolized by the character gaining dots in the Enhancement background, along with the Genetic Flaws).<br /> <br /> 2) I don't know for certain, but I would think that physical traits reflecting Attributes &gt;6 would depend more on the character's Paradigm. If it's a Progenitor or Etherite using medicine to bolster their muscle mass, then obviously they would look as swole as they are. If it's a mystic channeling the strength of Samson, the beasts of the wild, or the celestial bodies, the character would probably not look much different. After all, from their perspective, the strength they gain has nothing to do with their muscles.<br /> <br /> 3) I would assume &quot;these changes becoming permanent&quot; is the textbook definition of a Genetic Flaw. See item #1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-03T23:53:55-07:00","id":1137211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137056-a-question-about-boosting-attributes-using-life-3?p=1137126#post1137126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If it's a mystic channeling the strength of Samson, the beasts of the wild, or the celestial bodies, the character would probably not look much different. After all, from their perspective, the strength they gain has nothing to do with their muscles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmhmh. I disagree for one reason - it's the *Life* Sphere.<br /> Or rather, let me rephrase - I disagree that there are no physical changes either way. The Life sphere's domain are either changes to the invisible lifeforce, or changes to..well, the physical pattern. And the former does not quite give you increased strength despite the 'force' in its name.<br /> <br /> Now, this does not mean that the physical changes are *apparent* at first glance! The mystic might not get any visual changes for the same reason a Progenitor can avoid it (Though I agree that bulk change would be more common among Etherites and Progenitor treatments): The muscle internals become different. Instead of bulk, there are microscopic changes to the build, the structure. Perhaps downright alien changes.<br /> <br /> But either way, if you want strength without any physical changes of any way, that would fall under the Forces sphere IMO. And *there*, the mystic could indeed literally conjure the strength of Samson into them - in the form of the sheer force of his strength. With the forces sphere involved, the Technocrat approach would in that case probably be cybernetics.<br /> <br /> At least, that's my interpretation. I think a more obvious example would be: It's the same reason why an approach to get '<i>The sight of an eagle'</i> with the life sphere would definitely change the eyes at least internally - while a Forces or Correspondence based approach would not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-04-2017, 03:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-04T00:38:33-07:00","id":1137223,"title":"","content":"At the very least, having the Strength of Samson should make your hair grow very long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T06:49:15-07:00","id":1137659,"title":"","content":"So basically if my character is a hermetic whose paradigm has to do with mysticism and the like; then accordingly to the paradigm the body won't essentially change in a visible way, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","user":"MowtekPvP","date":". 09-05-2017, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-05T07:16:18-07:00","id":1137664,"title":"","content":"It depends on how do you describe the effect within your Paradigm: For instance, if the spell empowers you with &quot;the strength of Heracles&quot;, well, Heracles was burly, but not gigantic, and he certainly was WAY stronger than he looked...soo, maybe I will say that you gain muscular mass if you have little but not to a &quot;Hulk size&quot; (your body becomes similar to that of the legend to incarnate it's mystical potency). Other ways to justify your strenght may cause different effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-05-2017, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T14:12:22-07:00","id":1138107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137056-a-question-about-boosting-attributes-using-life-3?p=1137664#post1137664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on how do you describe the effect within your Paradigm: For instance, if the spell empowers you with &quot;the strength of Heracles&quot;, well, Heracles was burly, but not gigantic, and he certainly was WAY stronger than he looked...soo, maybe I will say that you gain muscular mass if you have little but not to a &quot;Hulk size&quot; (your body becomes similar to that of the legend to incarnate it's mystical potency). Other ways to justify your strenght may cause different effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I infact want to get 10 dex, however I'm not sure how should I describe the effect so it doesn't deform the body too much :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-06T15:34:53-07:00","id":1138124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1137056-a-question-about-boosting-attributes-using-life-3?p=1138107#post1138107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I infact want to get 10 dex, however I'm not sure how should I describe the effect so it doesn't deform the body too much :/</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds to me like you want to go diving without getting your face wet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-07T06:33:12-07:00","id":1138305,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it sounds like that.<br /> <br /> The method it's, I think:<br /> <br /> 1rst: Think how your mage will accomplish the feat within Paradigm.<br /> <br /> 2nd: After determining how your mage does it, you should have clues about how the effect would change your body (or not).<br /> <br /> 3rd: Think how to &quot;deal with it&quot; . And, if you can't deal with the consequences, don't do it.<br /> <br /> That being said, in my opinion, Dextrety it's far more ephemeral than Strenght as it has a lot to do with hand-eye coordination, reflexes, fine motor skills, and such.<br /> <i>I actually find hard to think how this will deform your body!</i>.<br /> I imagine superhuman Dextrety as someone that accomplishes every physical task with eery accuracy, every move that she does it's perfect and calculated, and she does that with incredibly fast reflexes. She also may be able to contort in bizarre ways, but that's all. It shouldn't seem too unhuman when the character isn't contorting in ways that defy understanding, or fighting with a martial artists while writting poetry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-07-2017, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}